# duel-core

Slice 1 of the plan after the walking skeleton: the pure, deterministic 1v1 duel simulation of `docs/spec.md` §7 and §8 with the Duelist kit, rollback-ready snapshots and a replay runner. It is the contract the combat spike (`duel-online`) builds on. It runs in parallel with `world-sea`, so it owns only new directories and three `package.json` files.

- `feature.json`: one lane (`duel`), the bundled reviewers, `prd` = `docs/spec.md`.
- `policy.json`: owned paths and four checks (typecheck, unit, integration, build); no browser check.
- `duel-task.md`: the lane's outcome brief.
- `decisions.md`: the operator's decisions.

Launch from `~/dev/project-B`: `workflow launch duel-core --dry-run`, then the launch line in `CLAUDE.md`.
